  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The output from a NAND gate having inputs A and B given below will be,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0049_7088dd95b0fd.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 148px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\ot1_0049_254be1f2afcc.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 98px;\" /></p>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\ot2_0049_f527fd017271.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 98px;\" /></p>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\ot3_0049_0f6d050385a7.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 100px;\" /></p>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\ot4_0049_92fc85eab32e.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 98px;\" /></p>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The output of NAND gate is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math>.</p><p>The truth table is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>A</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>B</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>Y</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math> would&nbsp;be zero only when both A&nbsp;and B&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> . Clearly, for all other input conditions the output will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>. Hence, this is the right option.</p></blockquote>"
  }
